# Name-level engagement scope for the egress relay (squid `scope_domains` ACL).
#
# One domain per line. An entry `example.com` is rendered as
# `acl scope_domains dstdomain .example.com`, which matches example.com and all of
# its subdomains. No leading dot, no scheme, no path.
#
# Copy to nftables/scope.domains.allow (gitignored) or to
# nftables/profiles/<engagement>/scope.domains.allow, then run:
#   ./scripts/render-squid-scope.sh --profile <engagement>
#
# WHY THIS IS A GENERATED FILE AND NOT A TRACKED ONE: the domain list names the
# client. It is engagement-confidential in exactly the way nftables/scope.allow is,
# and keeping it out of the repo means a fork or a publish cannot leak the target.
#
# EMPTY IS THE DEFAULT AND MEANS DENY. With no entries the ACL matches nothing and
# every scope-domain request is refused — the same posture as the empty nftables sets.
#
# example:
#   client.example
#   docs.client.example
